    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>A streamlined US shipping solution for WooCommerce and Pitney Bowes.</p>\n<h3>Features</h3>\n<p>&#9745;  <strong>Print US Domestic Labels</strong> by USPS, PB, FedEx or UPS</p>\n<p>&#9745; <strong>Live Customizable Rates</strong> in cart</p>\n<p>&#9745; <strong>Print Labels</strong> directly from WooCommerce orders</p>\n<p>&#9745; <strong>WooCommerce Shipment Tracking</strong> Compatible</p>\n<p>&#9745; <strong>Advanced Options</strong> for US address validation, insurance and special services</p>\n<p>&#9745; <strong>Delivery Notifications</strong> for customers and admins, plus support for SMS</p>\n<p>&#9745; <strong>Pitney Bowes business account</strong> required to purchase labels</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin files to the <code>/wp-content/plugins/pb-shipping</code> directory, or install the plugin through the WordPress plugins screen directly.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin through the \\&#8217;Plugins\\&#8217; screen in WordPress</li>\n<li>Go to the WooCommerce &gt; Settings page for setup</li>\n<li>Visit the WooCommerce &gt; Orders page to begin shipping orders</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='where%20can%20i%20get%20support%3F'>\nWhere can I get support?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Reach out to us anytime for <a href=\"https://richardlerma.com/#contact\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">additional support</a>.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>5.0.18</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility with WC 10.1. </li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.17</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Updates to allow 4 digit ins values.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.12</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor bug fixes</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.11</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Detect out of order acceptance scans. Improve predictive box sizes.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.9</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added delivery estimate to tracking meta.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.7</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Compatibility with WC 8.9, Added sanitization to setting tabs.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.6</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Report interface refinements.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.5</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Caching and report refinements.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.3</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor setup improvements. Revised fetch logic.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.1</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Minor aesthetic improvements.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Restructured account setup. Improved instructions.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
